Bug 2063939 - Fix signature not inserted below in plaintext forward.

  Inserting a br element into the empty div was a kludge at the time (Bug 1249884),
  not it turns out that it deletion fails with NS_ERROR_EDITOR_UNEXPECTED_DOM_TREE (0x80560002),
  so the best fix is to remove the hack altogether.

  We didn't check the AI alaysis:

  Root cause confirmed in M-C: DeleteNode() lands in EditorBase::DeleteNodeWithTransaction(),
  which refuses to remove any node failing HTMLEditUtils::IsRemovableNode() and returns NS_ERROR_EDITOR_UNEXPECTED_DOM_TREE:

    // Do nothing if the node is read-only.
    if (IsHTMLEditor() && NS_WARN_IF(!HTMLEditUtils::IsRemovableNode(aContent))) {
      return NS_ERROR_EDITOR_UNEXPECTED_DOM_TREE;
    }

  IsRemovableNode() only allows deleting nodes whose parent carries the NODE_IS_EDITABLE flag (or padding <br>s).
  The synthetic moz-forward-container div you insert programmatically apparently no longer gets that flag in the
  plaintext mail composer — that's why the sibling-<br> deletion (parent = editable body) still works,
  while extraBr (parent = the div) fails.

